WEBVTT

00:02.730 --> 00:03.640
Let's go!

00:05.820 --> 00:08.810
Go, Winged Warrior Justice!

00:08.810 --> 00:11.250
I'll take care of this all at once.

00:32.760 --> 00:35.900
Void response at 0%. 
The Void has been destroyed.

00:35.900 --> 00:37.780
Yahoo!

00:37.780 --> 00:42.490
Hm. It feels as though 
the Voids' power grows by the day.

00:44.520 --> 00:46.940
Ah, everything'll be fine.

00:46.940 --> 00:51.410
Because we, the Nine Soldiers, are here.

02:35.750 --> 02:39.870
Even if we slice through the Void's exterior,
 it just causes the liquid to expand,

02:39.870 --> 02:41.970
and it continues to move in liquid form.

02:42.790 --> 02:47.630
It evaded our attacks, got past our defenses,
and headed straight for the Soul Future.

02:48.800 --> 02:52.150
It solidified itself to the tower
 and stopped moving.

02:52.150 --> 02:55.030
Its exterior has only grown stronger,

02:55.030 --> 02:59.850
Luke tried his sword, and we tried
an all-out attack, too, but it did nothing.

02:59.850 --> 03:04.920
It remains at the same location 
and it is impossible to move it elsewhere.

03:04.920 --> 03:07.740
The area has been evacuated and closed off.

03:07.740 --> 03:11.520
Given the situation, 
we believe it is a chrysalis.

03:07.750 --> 03:12.500
Episode 6: CHANGE

03:11.520 --> 03:12.480
A chrysalis?

03:12.480 --> 03:19.760
Insects that undergo full metamorphosis enter 
a rest stage before the larva becomes an adult.

03:19.760 --> 03:25.480
So next time, it'll be in its final form
 and it will devour the Soul Future.

03:25.480 --> 03:27.770
That is what it means, yes.

03:29.150 --> 03:30.720
Then, before that happens...

03:32.260 --> 03:33.590
Where are you going?

03:33.590 --> 03:35.740
We need to slay it before it moves again.

03:35.740 --> 03:40.890
You just saw how it is. Even when 
we all attacked it, it didn't budge.

03:40.890 --> 03:41.980
That's why I—

03:41.980 --> 03:42.910
Sit down.

03:42.910 --> 03:46.630
If I knew it was going to liquefy, 
I would've drawn something else.

03:46.630 --> 03:50.040
I wouldn't have drawn a sword. 
In order to fight a liquid enemy...

03:51.590 --> 03:54.280
Well, I'll figure it out on the way there.

03:57.330 --> 03:58.970
You could've died!

04:00.200 --> 04:02.380
You almost died back there.

04:02.380 --> 04:03.780
Do you understand that?

04:08.300 --> 04:09.120
Luke!

04:37.530 --> 04:40.760
Well, well. If it isn't one of 
the esteemed Nine Soldiers.

04:40.760 --> 04:43.050
Never thought I'd run into you here.

04:49.420 --> 04:50.830
Good work.

05:03.320 --> 05:05.680
Well? You want a drink?

05:10.720 --> 05:13.650
So... Well, you know.

05:14.120 --> 05:17.400
I hear the current enemy's pretty tough.

05:17.400 --> 05:21.120
Guess it must be pretty hard to fight 
now that it's stuck to the tower.

05:21.720 --> 05:24.090
Even so, we will fight it.

05:28.890 --> 05:35.030
If this enemy ends up flying, 
the only one who can fight in the air is Unio.

05:35.420 --> 05:36.190
If you were there—

05:36.190 --> 05:39.110
I stopped fighting.

05:39.110 --> 05:41.190
Sorry, but I won't be able to help.

05:44.790 --> 05:49.570
You guys have done a great job lasting so long
 after the eighth Soul Future was taken.

05:49.570 --> 05:54.450
You think so, too, don't you, Chingosman?

05:54.450 --> 05:57.110
You make it sound like I'm going to lose.

05:57.110 --> 05:58.910
I'm going to win.

06:00.390 --> 06:01.640
No matter what.

06:01.640 --> 06:04.450
Well, don't dwell on it.

06:04.450 --> 06:08.850
Life is long. I'm sure even the legendary hero's
gotta lose every once in a while.

06:08.850 --> 06:09.960
I absolutely will not!

06:13.960 --> 06:19.680
If I lose, it'll mean the friends who fought
 alongside me will have died in vain.

06:19.970 --> 06:21.370
I am the hero.

06:21.610 --> 06:23.990
Don't compare me to some shitty lizard

06:23.990 --> 06:26.680
who ran from the fight with
 their tail between their legs!

06:28.010 --> 06:31.880
A shitty lizard who ran away with 
their tail between their legs, huh?

06:34.000 --> 06:35.760
That's a good one.

06:41.360 --> 06:42.200
Hey.

06:42.200 --> 06:43.370
Hm?

06:43.370 --> 06:45.790
What are those things you're eating?

06:46.570 --> 06:47.730
Want one?

06:47.730 --> 06:49.870
You idiot! Don't eat those!

06:49.870 --> 06:54.300
Chingosman always said never to 
eat the worms from the graveyard!

06:55.140 --> 06:57.720
The ones here are nice 
and plump and delicious.

06:59.620 --> 07:02.590
Seriously. You're unbelievable.

07:04.680 --> 07:06.850
How's that girlie doing?

07:08.310 --> 07:13.600
Hubris can get you killed. 
Though I'm sure she's been pretty helpful.

07:13.860 --> 07:17.240
Her summoning magic is 
like nothing I've ever seen before.

07:17.560 --> 07:21.210
Almost to the point where I think 
maybe if she'd been around from the start,

07:21.210 --> 07:24.000
not a single Soul Future 
would've been eaten.

07:24.000 --> 07:25.840
She's that reliable, huh?

07:26.260 --> 07:29.750
So I guess the ultimate soldier 
showed up in the nick of time—

07:29.750 --> 07:31.760
No, it's not that great.

07:31.760 --> 07:32.410
Huh?

07:32.410 --> 07:35.250
Ever since she showed up, 
our whole plan has been thrown off.

07:35.250 --> 07:40.150
She's inconsiderate, violent, arrogant, 
and nothing she does makes any sense.

07:40.150 --> 07:43.390
She's a stupid, reckless jerk 
who does nothing but make me worry.

07:43.390 --> 07:45.140
You still talking about that girl—

07:45.140 --> 07:47.700
It's Natsuko! Her name is Natsuko Hirose!

07:47.700 --> 07:48.780
Justice!

07:48.780 --> 07:50.550
Uh, what is it?

07:53.250 --> 07:54.520
Seriously, what?

07:55.060 --> 07:57.150
About this "adult" relationship...

07:57.150 --> 07:57.760
Huh?

07:57.760 --> 08:00.640
No, never mind. I don't want to know.

08:00.640 --> 08:04.380
Ugh. Seriously, what is her <i>problem</i>?

08:04.380 --> 08:06.270
Why do I have to do this?

08:06.740 --> 08:08.700
Ah, damn it!

08:08.700 --> 08:13.060
First off, she eats my food without 
permission, she never listens...

08:13.060 --> 08:15.170
Shouldn't you go after him?

08:13.490 --> 08:15.170
<i>And</i> you can't even see her face.

08:15.170 --> 08:16.880
Seriously, what's her deal?

08:16.480 --> 08:19.430
Your best friend sure is
going through some things.

08:16.880 --> 08:19.000
Seriously! Damn it!

08:19.430 --> 08:22.690
Tch. Shut up! Don't make fun of Luke!

08:22.690 --> 08:25.340
And stop eating those worms,
 you stupid dragon!

08:39.330 --> 08:45.210
<b>Insecticide Robot</b>

08:39.330 --> 08:45.210
<b>Insect Cage Man</b>

08:47.150 --> 08:49.710
Oil. Straight up.

08:57.900 --> 09:02.960
Natsuko. You were blown away by the Void, 
but you're completely unharmed.

09:03.940 --> 09:05.810
Do you know why that is?

09:10.090 --> 09:11.260
How is she?

09:11.260 --> 09:13.830
Unio, can you help me?

09:13.830 --> 09:16.370
Man, she's so much trouble.

09:22.140 --> 09:26.450
Please don't get the idea that 
you're defeating these Voids all by yourself.

09:29.250 --> 09:31.500
<b>Insecticide Robot</b>

09:29.250 --> 09:31.500
<b>Insect Cage Man</b>

09:31.510 --> 09:35.500
Don't act like you're making 
this all by yourself.

09:40.120 --> 09:43.590
I guess I don't mind listening to 
this so-called plan you all have.

09:43.590 --> 09:44.800
What?!

09:44.800 --> 09:46.760
I'll defeat the Voids, no matter what.

09:46.760 --> 09:48.660
How did you reach <i>that</i> conclusion?

09:48.660 --> 09:52.080
The human mind is impossible 
to understand. Totally impossible.

09:52.080 --> 09:55.750
I just want to defeat all the Voids.
 What's wrong with that?

09:55.750 --> 09:57.500
You seriously...

09:57.500 --> 10:00.990
This all would've been over long ago
 if Natsuko hadn't arrived.

10:00.990 --> 10:01.880
Oh?

10:01.880 --> 10:03.010
Memmeln?

10:03.010 --> 10:04.380
That's what I believe.

10:04.930 --> 10:11.120
If Natsuko hadn't appeared, this town and 
all of us would have been done for long ago.

10:12.200 --> 10:17.920
When I watch Natsuko fight, 
at times, it makes me anxious.

10:17.920 --> 10:22.800
She's reckless, foolhardy, 
and so desperate to protect something.

10:26.590 --> 10:29.890
It's all your fault.

10:32.480 --> 10:35.070
I don't want to lose anyone ever again.

10:35.560 --> 10:37.410
Natsuko, I want you to survive.

10:38.150 --> 10:41.180
Please believe in our strength, too.

10:41.180 --> 10:46.010
We won't be able to defeat this Void 
we're currently facing unless we work together.

10:47.540 --> 10:48.690
I understand.

10:49.110 --> 10:51.090
What exactly do you "understand"?

10:52.880 --> 10:56.120
I'll believe in all of you 
and work together with you.

11:01.080 --> 11:04.050
That is the correct answer. Good girl.

11:06.640 --> 11:10.910
Memmeln's sorta amazing. 
She managed to tame that wild beast.

11:12.430 --> 11:13.900
What are you doing?

11:13.900 --> 11:17.700
I've never seen Memmeln looking this cute, 
so I need to draw her before I forget.

11:17.700 --> 11:20.300
Me? Cute?

11:20.300 --> 11:22.200
Ooh, that expression's great, too!

11:22.200 --> 11:26.210
The reference material doesn't have too many 
of Memmeln's and Justice's expressions.

11:26.210 --> 11:27.720
Ah, she's so cute.

11:29.160 --> 11:32.200
Then, the reason you were 
drawing Justice was...

11:32.200 --> 11:35.020
I wanna draw all of these looks
 I've never seen before.

11:35.020 --> 11:36.080
That's it?

11:36.080 --> 11:37.170
That's it.

11:37.540 --> 11:41.270
Just so you know, I drew the heck 
outta you when I was little,

11:41.270 --> 11:43.710
so I can draw you with any expression
with my eyes closed.

11:45.200 --> 11:46.960
O-Oh.

11:46.960 --> 11:49.730
Uh-huh. I see.

11:50.700 --> 11:51.980
Luke?

11:51.980 --> 11:54.740
All right! Let's work together and fight.

11:55.480 --> 11:57.730
We produce reliability and results:

11:58.080 --> 12:01.740
Nine Soldiers!

12:06.280 --> 12:08.330
R-Right.

12:13.750 --> 12:16.860
This way, everyone. Stay calm.

12:16.860 --> 12:18.410
Please don't push.

12:18.410 --> 12:21.270
What's the point of evacuating 
when the world's gonna end?

12:21.270 --> 12:24.790
I guess the Nine Soldiers 
are finally going to lose.

12:32.590 --> 12:37.440
All this superficial defense will do
 is put people at ease,

12:37.440 --> 12:39.400
but I guess it's better than nothing.

12:39.400 --> 12:42.880
Elder Baobab, we've finished the evacuation.

12:43.640 --> 12:45.300
Then, it's finally time.

12:49.180 --> 12:51.900
This might really be the end.

12:55.140 --> 12:56.130
Right here.

12:57.370 --> 12:58.870
QJ, enhance.

13:00.920 --> 13:03.260
You can see something like a hole inside.

13:03.260 --> 13:05.040
Is that its mouth?

13:05.040 --> 13:06.880
So that must be its weak point.

13:08.380 --> 13:12.390
It's impossible to cut through 
its exterior even with Luke's sword.

13:12.390 --> 13:15.410
There's a possibility it'll be able
 to fly in its final form.

13:16.400 --> 13:19.470
Unio, Natsuko, and I will 
stay on standby above it.

13:19.930 --> 13:24.510
QJ will fly around with a fragment of 
the Soul Future and make it open its mouth.

13:24.800 --> 13:28.320
Memmeln will then use 
her control magic to halt it.

13:28.320 --> 13:31.790
Unio and I will attack it directly 
while Natsuko uses her summoning magic.

13:32.030 --> 13:34.010
We'll all attack together from above.

13:34.420 --> 13:39.500
My control magic can only restrain it for
three seconds. Please defeat it during that time.

13:39.500 --> 13:40.360
Got it.

13:40.760 --> 13:44.420
Let's beat that thing quick,
then go enjoy some good booze.

13:44.420 --> 13:45.660
Stop that.

13:45.660 --> 13:47.540
That's definitely a death flag.

14:27.540 --> 14:28.560
It's no use.

14:45.960 --> 14:47.070
It's coming.

15:02.610 --> 15:03.870
It's huge!

15:07.670 --> 15:08.580
QJ!

15:12.920 --> 15:13.700
Memmeln!

15:13.700 --> 15:14.850
It's fast.

15:29.160 --> 15:30.280
Luke!

15:38.740 --> 15:41.030
My horn broke off!

15:47.390 --> 15:49.260
Ow.

16:00.370 --> 16:01.830
Luke!

16:09.690 --> 16:11.050
Crap!

16:11.880 --> 16:13.910
Draw. You need to draw, Natsuko.

16:13.910 --> 16:15.400
I'll draw, so just hurry!

16:51.500 --> 16:54.000
Luke! Unio!

16:54.960 --> 16:56.040
Run!

16:57.810 --> 16:58.790
Luke!

17:25.190 --> 17:27.540
I can't see them. Where'd they go?

17:33.650 --> 17:35.030
Justice!

17:35.560 --> 17:37.440
Fly me up there.

17:37.440 --> 17:38.530
What?

17:39.110 --> 17:40.870
With my desk, please.

17:40.870 --> 17:42.220
Your desk?

17:42.220 --> 17:44.240
Hey, I can't fly—

17:43.500 --> 17:45.990
Please. Up where I can see Luke and Unio.

17:51.340 --> 17:52.870
You don't need to fly fast.

17:52.870 --> 17:53.910
Just float up.

17:56.880 --> 17:59.990
Are we really gonna see 
the Nine Soldiers win from here?

18:07.760 --> 18:09.390
It's Justice!

18:09.390 --> 18:14.550
Justice! Justice! 
The Winged Warrior, Justice!

18:26.380 --> 18:28.000
More to the right.

18:28.000 --> 18:29.500
Get in a bit closer.

18:40.320 --> 18:45.400
Justice! You've got this!

18:54.020 --> 18:55.360
Justice?

19:04.210 --> 19:07.340
Justice... Wait, are you unable to fly?

19:08.460 --> 19:10.290
I said more to the right.

19:10.290 --> 19:13.230
You sure are rough with 
your dragons, little lady.

19:13.700 --> 19:14.960
I see them.

19:22.290 --> 19:23.630
The stairs!

19:27.400 --> 19:28.590
Luke!

19:44.860 --> 19:46.330
The barrier!

19:51.030 --> 19:52.410
QJ?

19:52.410 --> 19:56.170
"Kill... this... thing... dead... now."

19:57.080 --> 20:02.670
The beam lighting up five times 
is a sign to kill you dead!

20:10.900 --> 20:13.030
I can't fly, but...

20:14.360 --> 20:17.720
Fly, Luke!

20:30.100 --> 20:32.170
Controlele...

20:32.490 --> 20:33.670
Magi!

20:53.980 --> 20:57.680
Void response at 0%. 
The Void has been destroyed.

20:58.510 --> 21:00.930
They did it!

21:01.490 --> 21:04.820
Where's Memmeln and QJ? Is everyone here?

21:04.820 --> 21:08.010
Yeah. Luke and Unio are safe, as well.

21:09.740 --> 21:12.150
Good work, everyone.

21:26.980 --> 21:28.060
Justice!

21:28.060 --> 21:29.360
It's really Justice!

21:29.360 --> 21:30.710
So cool!

21:30.710 --> 21:31.900
Can I get your autograph?

21:31.900 --> 21:33.080
Ah! It's Unio!

21:33.080 --> 21:35.230
Unio!

21:48.480 --> 21:51.910
Why didn't you tell me about your wings?

21:52.300 --> 21:55.210
I don't like having others worry about me.

21:55.210 --> 22:02.530
Not to mention, a dragon that can't fly 
or breathe fire is the lamest thing ever.

22:05.290 --> 22:06.270
Seriously...

22:07.020 --> 22:08.270
You're such an idiot.

22:10.010 --> 22:12.030
I see now.

22:12.560 --> 22:17.840
So she's the ultimate warrior that managed 
to open up our great hero's heart.

23:50.030 --> 23:54.940
<b>Episode 7: "FIRST LOVE"</b>

23:50.030 --> 23:54.940
<b>Episode 7: "FIRST LOVE"</b>
